__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Large, regenerable local artifacts - never commit these. Each one has
# caused an accidental multi-GB commit (rejected by GitHub, since fixed by
# resetting local history) when added via `git add -A`/the GitHub web
# upload UI, which does not respect this file the way `git add` does.
# Regenerate them locally instead of committing them:
#   - checkpoints/                    -> experiments/filter_training (see docs/status_and_decisions.md)
#   - alzheimer_corpus_pilot/         -> a local sample of alzheimer_corpus/data/chunks/chunks.jsonl
#   - experiments/outputs/index_pilot_reduced_scope/ -> experiments/retrieval/build_index.py
# Small, legitimate result files (experiments/outputs/fit_and_evaluate/,
# the current result - see docs/status_and_decisions.md SS1.2) are NOT
# covered by a blanket experiments/outputs/ rule - a real committed
# result must stay visible to `git status`, not silently ignored
# alongside the large regenerable folders sitting next to it.
checkpoints/
alzheimer_corpus_pilot/
experiments/outputs/index_pilot_reduced_scope/
